+# Headless PPTX preservation patch
+
+Local branch `byteowlz/headless-pptx`, based on upstream
+`9859da39255c0262cd592bb57101d7f2fa961f72`. Tracker: sldr `trx-4s9s.25`.
+This is not an upstream release, rebranding, packaging completion or general
+PowerPoint compatibility certification. Upstream licenses and attribution remain unchanged.
+
+## Defects and fixes
+
+1. The shared shape reader discarded unknown `cNvPr/extLst` entries, while the
+   writer regenerated only hyperlinks and the decorative flag. Consequently,
+   presentation-level custom XML survived but its per-shape identity references
+   did not. `Shape.raw_cnvpr_ext` now carries relationship-free entries through
+   import, serde/native storage and export. Entries retain namespace bindings;
+   the writer combines them with the editable decorative marker in one list.
+2. The picture reader collapsed an omitted `rotWithShape` attribute into its
+   boolean value and the writer always emitted an explicit attribute. Even after
+   identity preservation this changed the source structure on a no-edit save.
+   `PictureFill.implicit_rotation` now retains source omission. Explicit true and
+   false still survive; requesting upright still writes an override. Newly
+   authored pictures and old native models keep their existing serialization.
+
+No consumer identity is interpreted, generated or reconstructed. Relationship-bearing
+opaque entries are not copied without relationship remapping. This bounded
+preservation path does not claim support for arbitrary unknown Office extensions.
+The two model fields are optional/defaulted for old native documents.
+
+## Regression coverage
+
+`nonvisual_extensions` exercises generated multi-slide metadata through the public
+PPTX API, serde/native-model storage and two saves. It checks resolved namespaces,
+including sibling prefix rebinding and inherited default namespaces, unique retained
+identities, no dangling relationship entry, no duplicate list and removal of stale
+modelled decoration. Old native shape JSON still loads.
+
+`picture_defaults` checks absent, explicit true and explicit false source properties
+through two saves, and an explicit upright edit after importing an omitted property.
+Both defect tests were observed failing before their respective fixes.
+
+```bash
+just check-headless
+just test-headless
+cargo fmt -p deckcraft-model -p deckcraft-pptx -- --check
+cargo clippy --locked -p deckcraft-model -p deckcraft-format \
+  -p deckcraft-pptx -p deckcraft-engine --all-targets -- -D warnings
+```
+
+Measured on macOS arm64 / Rust 1.97.0: check passes; **572 tests pass, one ignored**.
+Strict Clippy fails on the unchanged upstream
+`crates/model/src/trendline.rs:468` (`manual_range_contains`), reproduced on the
+unmodified base. A second run excluding only that lint via the command line
+(`-D warnings -A clippy::manual_range_contains`) passes. No source suppression or
+unrelated trendline fix is included. This is not full desktop/WASM CI.
+
+## Real sldr CLI proof
+
+Using the original synthetic three-slide fixture documented in sldr's
+`docs/pptx-spike/deckcraft-parity.md`, with sldr `0.10.0 (8fbbf2a7a)` unchanged:
+
+- All **17 shape identities**, three slide identities and the custom XML survive.
+- No-edit PPTX save and native `.deckcraft` save/reopen both pass strict
+  `sldr import --apply --dry-run` with no edits.
+- `text.replace` changes one sentence; dry-run writes nothing and real apply
+  changes exactly that sentence in exactly one disposable Markdown file.
+- Deliberately removed/duplicated identities and changed picture geometry still
+  fail strict import. No sldr validation was weakened.
+- All three direct PNG renders are byte-identical to the unmodified provider.
+
+Only disposable synthetic libraries were written. No private deck, proprietary
+font, PowerPoint-generated fixture or vendor screenshot is included. Actual
+PowerPoint open/save, arbitrary shape edits, clipboard duplication and full
+cross-renderer fidelity remain separately qualified capabilities.
